{"id": "PRR_kwDODtfaXs8AAAABLetVKw", "state": "COMMENTED", "body": "## CARE Review \u2014 adds multi-report support to service requests\n\n**What it does.** Replaces the \"one latest diagnostic report per service request\" model with a list: `DiagnosticReportForm` now renders a `DiagnosticReportItem` per report (each with its own `fullReport`/`files` queries, expansion state, and batched save), `DiagnosticReportReview` mirrors that for the review/approve side, expansion state is lifted into `ServiceRequestShow` so form and review stay in sync, and a new `MultipleDiagnosticReportsPrint` page fans out over all reports for a combined printout. Confidence: **high** \u2014 the restructure is legible and the per-report component split is the right shape for this.\n\n### Findings (4 inline)\n\n| # | Severity | Where | Issue |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `Broken` | `DiagnosticReportReview.tsx:177` | Conclusion reseed lost its guard \u2014 a refetch overwrites in-progress typing |\n| 2 | `Broken` | `DiagnosticReportForm.tsx:440` | Same reseeding hazard for conclusion + observations |\n| 3 | `Broken` | `FacilityRoutes.tsx:103` | New org print route missing `:` on `organizationId` (copied from existing block); also appears unlinked |\n| 4 | `Convention` | `DiagnosticReportForm.tsx:962` (+ review ~295) | Icon-only chevron / `MoreVertical` buttons have no `aria-label` |\n\nFindings 1 and 2 are the ones I'd actually act on: they were near-harmless when only one report existed, and this PR is what makes them reachable.\n\n### Verified non-findings\n\n- **Batch save is sound.** `useBatchRequest` routes each failed sub-request through the global error handler and the backend applies the batch atomically, so the atomicity claim in the description holds \u2014 no silent-failure finding here.\n- **`clearFiles` memoisation** (`useFileUpload.tsx`) is correct: the `useCallback` with `[]` deps is exactly what makes the consumer's effect dep array stable.\n- **`instanceId` in `FileUploadDialog`** is optional, only prefixes DOM ids, and leaves existing callers untouched \u2014 the right minimal fix for the duplicate-id collisions that appear once several report cards render at once.\n- Mutations without `onError` are fine: `mutate()` toasts on 400/406 globally and `silent` isn't set.\n\n### Approach & simplicity\n\nProportionate overall \u2014 the per-report component extraction is smaller than threading indices through the old single-report code would have been, and the change reuses `query()`/`mutate()`, `useBatchRequest` and the existing shadcn primitives rather than inventing anything.\n\nOne advisory (no change requested): `DiagnosticReportItem` and `DiagnosticReportReviewItem` now carry near-identical Collapsible/CardHeader/Avatar/Badge/chevron/dropdown chrome. They solve different problems (edit vs. review), so merging them would be false reuse \u2014 but if the headers drift, a shared presentational header would be the cheaper place to fix it.\n\nSmall question on `WorkflowProgress.tsx`: the sort flipped to descending with `index === 0` as \"latest\", and the key became `` `${event.timestamp}-${event.title}` ``. With multiple reports created in the same request, could two events share a timestamp *and* title? If so the key collides. Low confidence \u2014 flagging rather than asserting.\n\n> Generated by [CARE PR Reviewer](https://github.com/ohcnetwork/care_fe/actions/runs/33380803037) for #16455 \u00b7 opus50 \u00b7 348.1 AIC \u00b7 \u2316 3.84 AIC \u00b7 \u229e 20.3K\n\n<!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: CARE PR Reviewer, engine: copilot, model: claude-opus-5, id: 33380803037, workflow_id: care-review, run: https://github.com/ohcnetwork/care_fe/actions/runs/33380803037 -->\n\n<!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: ohcnetwork/care_fe/care-review -->", "submittedAt": "2026-08-31T10:18:20Z", "author": {"login": "github-actions"}}
{"id": "PRR_kwDODtfaXs8AAAABLfM_8g", "state": "COMMENTED", "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nCopilot reviewed 14 out of 14 changed files in this pull request and generated no new comments.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suppressed comments (2)</summary>\n\n**src/pages/Facility/services/serviceRequests/components/DiagnosticReportReview.tsx:140**\n* `files` are fetched for every report card on initial render, even when the card is collapsed. With multiple reports this creates unnecessary network traffic; fetching files only when expanded keeps the UI responsive and reduces load.\n```\n  const { data: files = { results: [], count: 0 }, isFetched: isFilesFetched } =\n    useQuery({\n      queryKey: [\"files\", \"diagnostic_report\", report.id],\n      queryFn: query.paginated(fileApi.list, {\n        queryParams: {\n```\n**src/Routers/routes/FacilityRoutes.tsx:98**\n* The organization print routes are missing the `:` in `:organizationId` (currently `\"/organization/organizationId/...\"`). This prevents these routes from matching and makes the print pages unreachable via organization context.\n```\n  ...[\n    \"/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/service_request/:serviceRequestId/diagnostic_reports/print\",\n    \"/organization/organizationId/patient/:patientId/service_request/:serviceRequestId/diagnostic_reports/print\",\n  ].reduce((acc: AppRoutes, path) => {\n```\n</details>\n\n", "submittedAt": "2026-08-31T11:25:41Z", "author": {"login": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer"}}
{"id": "PRR_kwDODtfaXs8AAAABLfPgaw", "state": "COMMENTED", "body": "## CARE Review \u2014 multiple diagnostic reports per service request\n\n**What this does:** reworks the service-request diagnostic-report flow from *one report* to *many*. `DiagnosticReportForm` and `DiagnosticReportReview` are each split into a container plus a per-report card (`DiagnosticReportItem` / `DiagnosticReportReviewItem`); `ServiceRequestShow` lifts an `expandedReport` signal so a card just saved in the form auto-expands in the review; a new `MultipleDiagnosticReportsPrint` route + extracted `DiagnosticReportPrintPreview` renders all `final` reports (with their files) in one printable document; `WorkflowProgress` gets per-report timeline entries, newest-first, with a \"latest\" badge. Confidence: **high** \u2014 the split reads cleanly and the new components are named for what they do.\n\n**The approach is proportionate.** Splitting each screen into container + item is the right shape for the problem, the print preview was correctly *extracted* rather than duplicated, and `useBatchRequest` keeps the observation + conclusion save atomic. A few nice touches worth calling out: `id`/`htmlFor` collisions are now instance-scoped via `instanceId`/`inputId`, `clearFiles` was given a stable identity so the effect dep is honest, and the `[\"files\", \"diagnostic_report\", id]` invalidations are now scoped instead of blowing away all files.\n\n### Findings\n\n- **`Broken`** \u2014 new print route registers `\"/organization/organizationId/...\"` (missing `:`), so the organization variant can never match. (Copied from two pre-existing occurrences above it.)\n- **`Broken` (confirm intent)** \u2014 \"Mark as complete\" is now disabled whenever *any* report is non-`final`, while the footbar still shows once *one* report is final. A request with an abandoned/never-finalized report becomes uncompletable with no UI escape hatch.\n- **`Broken` \u2014 verify** \u2014 `format(report.modified_date, ...)` passes a `string` straight to date-fns v4; only ISO-8601 parses, and this renders in every collapsed card header.\n- **Approach** \u2014 the review list fetches `fullReport` + `files` for every report unconditionally (2N requests on mount) while the form gates the identical queries on `isExpanded`.\n- **`Convention` (a11y)** \u2014 icon-only `MoreVertical` dropdown triggers (both files) and the expand/collapse chevron have no accessible name; `careui.instructions.md` requires labelled controls on medical data.\n- **`Polish`** \u2014 `reports_pending_final_review` interpolates a count without i18next plural variants.\n\nNothing here blocks the design of the change \u2014 the route typo and the mark-as-complete gate are the two I'd want resolved before merge. Everything else is a judgement call for the author.\n\n_On the earlier bot threads:_ the `id=\"conclusion\"` collision and the `as any` file type both look addressed in the current head, so those are fine.\n\n> Generated by [CARE PR Reviewer](https://github.com/ohcnetwork/care_fe/actions/runs/33386420065) for #16455 \u00b7 opus50 \u00b7 455.8 AIC \u00b7 \u2316 3 AIC \u00b7 \u229e 20.3K\n\n<!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: CARE PR Reviewer, engine: copilot, model: claude-opus-5, id: 33386420065, workflow_id: care-review, run: https://github.com/ohcnetwork/care_fe/actions/runs/33386420065 -->\n\n<!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: ohcnetwork/care_fe/care-review -->", "submittedAt": "2026-08-31T11:31:25Z", "author": {"login": "github-actions"}}
